--TEST--
`startsWith`, `endsWith` and `contains` throw `LogicError` for an empty value, `all` and `any` throw it with no filter, and every constructor that takes an attribute agrees with `equals` on which names it throws for — ADR 0278 § 6
--FILE--
<?nvs
// An empty part would match every value, so the three substring constructors throw.
int $empty = 0;
try { Core\Ldap\Filter::startsWith("cn", ""); } catch (LogicError $e) { $empty = $empty + 1; }
try { Core\Ldap\Filter::endsWith("cn", ""); } catch (LogicError $e) { $empty = $empty + 1; }
try { Core\Ldap\Filter::contains("cn", ""); } catch (LogicError $e) { $empty = $empty + 1; }
echo "empty values thrown: ", $empty, " of 3\n";
try {
    Core\Ldap\Filter::contains("cn", "");
} catch (LogicError $e) {
    echo $e->message, "\n";
}

// `all` and `any` need one filter or more.
try {
    Core\Ldap\Filter::all();
} catch (LogicError $e) {
    echo $e->message, "\n";
}
try {
    Core\Ldap\Filter::any();
} catch (LogicError $e) {
    echo $e->message, "\n";
}

// Every constructor throws for the same names `equals` throws for.
array<string> $bad = ["cn=x)(cn=*", "1cn", "", "cn;"];
int $thrown = 0;
foreach ($bad as var $name) {
    try { Core\Ldap\Filter::startsWith($name, "x"); } catch (LogicError $e) { $thrown = $thrown + 1; }
    try { Core\Ldap\Filter::endsWith($name, "x"); } catch (LogicError $e) { $thrown = $thrown + 1; }
    try { Core\Ldap\Filter::contains($name, "x"); } catch (LogicError $e) { $thrown = $thrown + 1; }
    try { Core\Ldap\Filter::atLeast($name, "x"); } catch (LogicError $e) { $thrown = $thrown + 1; }
    try { Core\Ldap\Filter::atMost($name, "x"); } catch (LogicError $e) { $thrown = $thrown + 1; }
    try { Core\Ldap\Filter::approx($name, "x"); } catch (LogicError $e) { $thrown = $thrown + 1; }
}
echo "bad names thrown: ", $thrown, " of ", Core\Arr::count($bad) * 6, "\n";
--EXPECT--
empty values thrown: 3 of 3
Core\Ldap\Filter::contains: the value is empty. `present` matches every entry with a value
Core\Ldap\Filter::all: there is no filter. Give one filter or more
Core\Ldap\Filter::any: there is no filter. Give one filter or more
bad names thrown: 24 of 24
